-**The group's translation of the interface** (T37-30, its second share; N669; DEC-127 (1), (2), (5), DEC-157 (1)–(6), DEC-179; K1793, K1804, K2200, K2201) Terms. A **word** is an entry of the word list (R68), known by its `key`. A word's **state** in a language is `missing` (nothing adopted), `shown` (an adoption members see) or `awaiting` (an adopted protected word waiting for its second check, members seeing the English); a stored draft (R67) is no state of the word. A **granted speaker** of a language is an administrator or a member holding a live grant for it (R69). Every act here is refused to a machine `by`, the assistant included (`MACHINE_CANNOT_TRANSLATE`; `record-grammar` R50: machine work can draft a translation and never adopt or confirm one), and refuses a `language` `jurisdictions.isLocale` does not accept `LANGUAGE_MALFORMED` (R64) and a key not in the word list `NO_SUCH_WORD`. Each new code takes the next free number of this module's families and awaits T38's stamp.
-- **R68** (DEC-179; T39, N807: the list itself moved to `setup-words` R1–R3) `INTERFACE_WORDS` is `setup-words`' `WORD_ROWS` (its R1) in its order, each row exported as `{key, en, note, means, protected}`, the list and each word frozen; `INTERFACE_WORDS_COMMIT` is its `WORDS_COMMIT` (its R2). This module holds no copy of the list. A word keeps its key when its English changes (DEC-179 (3)): every adoption records the English it translated, and R74 answers `english_changed: true` for a shown word whose recorded English is not the list's.
-- **R69** (DEC-157 (1)) `translationGrant({member, language, revoke?, by})` (`op=translationgrant`): an administrator grants a named active member the right to translate the interface into `language`, or with `revoke: true` revokes it. Refusals in order, each writing nothing: `MACHINE_CANNOT_TRANSLATE`; `NOT_AN_ADMIN` (`membership` R84); `LANGUAGE_MALFORMED`; `NO_SUCH_MEMBER` for a `member` that is absent, a machine identity or not active, answered through `membership`'s `noSuchMember` (its R121, C-96.47) with `member` the id asked. A grant is recorded with the administrator and instant; a revocation is appended, never a deletion; a second grant of a live grant, or a second revocation, answers `existed: true` with the first. A grant is live while it is not revoked and its member is active. `translationGranted({member, language})` (in-process) answers whether `member` is a granted speaker of `language`, for R67 and R70–R73.
-- **R70** (DEC-127 (5), DEC-157 (2)–(4)) `translationAdopt({language, key, text, draft?, by})` (`op=translationadopt`): a granted speaker keeps a word's translation, typed or from a stored draft (`draft`, R67's id, kept as drafted or corrected). Refusals in order, each writing nothing: `MACHINE_CANNOT_TRANSLATE`; `LANGUAGE_MALFORMED`; `TRANSLATION_NOT_GRANTED`; `NO_SUCH_WORD`; `NO_SUCH_DRAFT` for a `draft` that is not a stored draft of that key and language; `TRANSLATION_TEXT_REFUSED` for a `text` that is not 1 to 2,000 characters on one line, or whose placeholders (`{name}`) differ from the English's. The adoption is recorded `{language, key, text, en, by, at, replaced, draft}` (`replaced` the text it replaces, or null for the English). An ordinary word is then `shown`, to every member reading `language` at once. A protected word is `shown` only when `text` is exactly the stored draft named by `draft` (kept as the assistant drafted it, one speaker's keeping enough; K2200 (1)); changed from that draft, or typed without one, it is `awaiting` (R71) and members see the English until it is confirmed. It answers `{ok: true, language, key, state}`.
