+- **R4** (moved from `instance-setup` R70; T50; N1084; DEC-127 (5), DEC-157 (2)–(4)) `translationAdopt({language, key, text, draft?, by})` (`op=translationadopt`): a granted speaker keeps a word's translation, typed or from a stored draft (`draft`, R1's id, kept as drafted or corrected). Refusals in order, each writing nothing: `MACHINE_CANNOT_TRANSLATE`; `LANGUAGE_MALFORMED`; `TRANSLATION_NOT_GRANTED`; `NO_SUCH_WORD`; `NO_SUCH_DRAFT` for a `draft` that is not a stored draft of that key and language; `TRANSLATION_TEXT_REFUSED` for a `text` that is not 1 to 2,000 characters on one line, or whose placeholders (`{name}`) differ from the English's. The adoption is recorded `{language, key, text, en, by, at, replaced, draft}` (`replaced` the text it replaces, or null for the English). An ordinary word is then `shown`, to every member reading `language` at once. A protected word is `shown` only when `text` is exactly the stored draft named by `draft` (kept as the assistant drafted it, one speaker's keeping enough; K2200 (1)); changed from that draft, or typed without one, it is `awaiting` (R5) and members see the English until it is confirmed. It answers `{ok: true, language, key, state}`. *(not yet met: T50)*
+- **R5** (moved from `instance-setup` R71; T50; N1084; DEC-157 (4)) `translationConfirm({language, key, by})` (`op=translationconfirm`) confirms an `awaiting` protected word, which is then `shown`. It is confirmed by a granted speaker of `language` who is not the member who adopted it, or by an administrator, whose confirmation is their own act after reading the assistant's translation of the word back into English (R1's `to_english`). (K2216) An administrator's confirmation of a protected word changed from the draft or typed without one is refused `TRANSLATION_NOT_READ_BACK` (a sentence saying the word has not been read back into English for its current text, then the remedy: read it back into English first) unless R1 holds a reading by that administrator for that key and language whose SHA-256 is that of the word's current kept text; a second granted speaker needs none. Refusals in order, each writing nothing: `MACHINE_CANNOT_TRANSLATE`; `LANGUAGE_MALFORMED`; `TRANSLATION_NOT_GRANTED`; `NO_SUCH_WORD`; `TRANSLATION_NOT_AWAITING` (the word is not `awaiting`); `TRANSLATION_CONFIRM_SELF` (the adopter, unless an administrator); `TRANSLATION_NOT_READ_BACK` (an administrator with no such reading, K2216). The confirmation is recorded with who and when beside the adoption. *(not yet met: T50)*
